{"title":"1983 AHSME Problems/Problem 30","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AHSME_Problems/Problem_30&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Distinct points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> are on a semicircle with diameter <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/c/bbcfabd65745f2b759dea1840f9a0753b2f992e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MN$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> and center <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. \nThe point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/3/ba369b33271c6fb52789f86292cc68559a2e0411.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CN$\" width=\"31\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/0/1e06eee59550afe91de41e236d33c4516a0a12dc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle CAP = \\angle CBP = 10^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"183\" height=\"13\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/8/458e043c0f22d1503fd5c6366a01f3ae05920309.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\stackrel{\\frown}{MA} = 40^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"76\" height=\"21\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/a/1ba61f76f6db42348dd5c407946a8657ed71662d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\stackrel{\\frown}{BN}$\" width=\"31\" height=\"20\" /> equals\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/8/6f8eeadd8cd1dc376957cf77a425565771406dee.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] import geometry; import graph;  unitsize(2 cm);  pair A, B, C, M, N, P;  M = (-1,0); N = (1,0); C = (0,0); A = dir(140); B = dir(20); P = extension(A, A + rotate(10)*(C - A), B, B + rotate(10)*(C - B));  draw(M--N); draw(arc(C,1,0,180)); draw(A--C--B); draw(A--P--B);  label(&quot;$A$&quot;, A, NW); label(&quot;$B$&quot;, B, E); label(&quot;$C$&quot;, C, S); label(&quot;$M$&quot;, M, SW); label(&quot;$N$&quot;, N, SE); label(&quot;$P$&quot;, P, S); [/asy]\" width=\"242\" height=\"118\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/a/2ea4ae0ae600da26f1d4cb1d3282d6e4e0353c91.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 10^{\\circ}\\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ 15^{\\circ}\\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ 20^{\\circ}\\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ 25^{\\circ}\\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ 30^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"431\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AHSME_Problems/Problem_30&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/a/b7a484f612628cf5710f1d36a2dd8206f27e688c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle CAP = \\angle CBP = 10^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"183\" height=\"13\" />, quadrilateral <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/3/483ba22e67c264e00ea32fab6c565093bb12cf17.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABPC$\" width=\"56\" height=\"13\" /> is cyclic (as shown below) by the converse of the theorem \"angles inscribed in the same arc are equal\".\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/9/5e9cc38e0a2a07d2d92807cc79ced537fe66d8ea.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] import geometry; import graph;  unitsize(2 cm);  pair A, B, C, M, N, P;  M = (-1,0); N = (1,0); C = (0,0); A = dir(140); B = dir(20); P = extension(A, A + rotate(10)*(C - A), B, B + rotate(10)*(C - B));  draw(M--N); draw(arc(C,1,0,180)); draw(A--C--B); draw(A--P--B); draw(A--B); draw(circumcircle(A,B,C),dashed);  label(&quot;$A$&quot;, A, NW); label(&quot;$B$&quot;, B, E); label(&quot;$C$&quot;, C, S); label(&quot;$M$&quot;, M, SW); label(&quot;$N$&quot;, N, SE); label(&quot;$P$&quot;, P, S); [/asy]\" width=\"242\" height=\"212\" />\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/f/8afe004241c469fadef9f654f6d5f028b8f29538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ACM = 40^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"108\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/8/408b74d41f5753df378f9956140362964445bf17.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ACP = 140^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"112\" height=\"13\" />, so, using the fact that opposite angles in a cyclic quadrilateral sum to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/0/3f0cd95f95238159d02dbcea0aca632c2928991c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$180^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"37\" height=\"15\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/2/602963fdbbefdc88f956dbc032f785974fda9c1a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ABP = 40^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"103\" height=\"13\" />. Hence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/2/ac29422680d09e955bfe74536364b1df7b197d25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ABC = \\angle ABP - \\angle CBP = 40^ \\circ - 10^\\circ = 30^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"363\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/a/25ac34b586e5bf479996d1326324bcf284ed54ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CA = CB$\" width=\"80\" height=\"13\" />, triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> is isosceles, with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/0/56067c4496d5e765b361a3bbacb4701417912450.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BAC = \\angle ABC = 30^\\circ$\" width=\"183\" height=\"13\" />. Now, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/f/7ff37de062292307fde8ce10ec3210d638937cdc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BAP = \\angle BAC - \\angle CAP = 30^\\circ - 10^\\circ = 20^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"358\" height=\"13\" />. Finally, again using the fact that angles inscribed in the same arc are equal, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/e/8de1c1e6b7bff110ee6d9f10207a1cd597a7041b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BCP = \\angle BAP = \\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}\\ 20^{\\circ}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"231\" height=\"29\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AHSME_Problems/Problem_30&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/e/71e94e42359b1b42761658d47e74985f2ad82da7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] import geometry; import graph;  unitsize(4 cm);  pair A, B, C, M, N, P, Q, R;  M = (-1,0); N = (1,0); C = (0,0); A = dir(140); B = dir(20); Q = dir(-20); R = dir(-40); P = extension(A, A + rotate(10)*(C - A), B, B + rotate(10)*(C - B));  draw(M--N); draw(circle(C,1)); draw(A--C--B); draw(A--P--B); draw(A--Q--C); draw(A--R--C); draw(A--B); draw(B--Q);  label(&quot;$A$&quot;, A, NW); label(&quot;$B$&quot;, B, E); label(&quot;$C$&quot;, C, SW); label(&quot;$M$&quot;, M, SW); label(&quot;$N$&quot;, N, SE); label(&quot;$P$&quot;, P, S); label(&quot;$Q$&quot;, Q, SE); label(&quot;$R$&quot;, R, SE); [/asy]\" width=\"432\" height=\"382\" />\n</p><p>Complete the circle centered at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and extend <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/b/e3bb4eeb347e74e025fd175c22f1f7275af0555e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AP$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> to meet the circle at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, respectively.  So <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/4/244ca47c2ece779743333f7cb6af79b7daad37e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\stackrel{\\frown}{NR} = \\stackrel{\\frown}{MA} = 40^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"125\" height=\"24\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/5/4e531406883ff6d3a11c3194385dcf61038c1884.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\stackrel{\\frown}{QR} = 2 \\cdot 10^\\circ = 20^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"147\" height=\"27\" />.  Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/7/1271bf5641971897eb4cd5cdfa32f3e149c48096.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\stackrel{\\frown}{NQ} = 40^\\circ - 20^\\circ = 20^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"176\" height=\"27\" />.  \n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/a/11ad8b32344788904404b1d198666c37ec7ccf27.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CA = CQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"83\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/2/c8212676796838c33dfb6cc84ada281c8cf6f4b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle CAQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"60\" height=\"18\" /> is isosceles and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/2/33212d6334f1b9038da129bd2cd09719f0e652f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle CQA = \\angle CAQ = 10^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"186\" height=\"18\" />.  Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/5/8650e79c1c48024a584861921f1d9f071ab8e677.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta = \\angle CBQ = \\angle CQB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"172\" height=\"18\" />.  Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/6/396eba089e04a4c33b59c46eddd0174d86899a7a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle PBQ = \\angle PQB = \\theta - 10^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"220\" height=\"18\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/0/ce0d02ec52155205aa2ea82d3b28a7b5354f57fc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle PBQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> is isosceles with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/c/6dcc84ab5fa4d59f0af1a50d62af721712a8239a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PB = PQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"84\" height=\"18\" />.  So <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/3/ba369b33271c6fb52789f86292cc68559a2e0411.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CN$\" width=\"31\" height=\"12\" /> must bisect <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/5/2e58a05f5146b687fbad5bf8b9679d93fb009d87.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BCQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"58\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/a/95a7eea7932c0785af922a4550ee15f9b4ce29f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\stackrel{\\frown}{BN} = \\stackrel{\\frown}{NQ} = \\boxed{(\\mathbf{C})\\ 20^{\\circ}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"169\" height=\"34\" />.\n</p><p>-j314andrews\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AHSME_Problems/Problem_30&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/fZAChuJDlSw?si=wJUPmgVRlYwazauh\">https://youtu.be/fZAChuJDlSw?si=wJUPmgVRlYwazauh</a>\n</p><p>~ smartschoolboy9\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AHSME_Problems/Problem_30&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AHSME\" title=\"1983 AHSME\">1983 AHSME</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1983 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1983 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1983\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AHSME_Problems/Problem_29\" title=\"1983 AHSME Problems/Problem 29\">Problem 29</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b>Last Problem</b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1983 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1983 AHSME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AHSME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1983 AHSME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AHSME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1983 AHSME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AHSME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1983 AHSME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AHSME_Problems/Problem_6\" t